# What a local `vercel deploy` must not upload.
#
# CI never needs this file: the workflow checks out from git and ships
# `vercel deploy --prebuilt`, so it only ever uploads .vercel/output. This is
# for deploying from a working tree by hand.
#
# The testimonial videos are the reason it exists. gary-cucchi.mp4 is 179 MB and
# ned-schaut.mp4 is 104 MB, both over Vercel's 100 MB per-file limit, so a plain
# `vercel deploy` pushes 277 MB and then fails outright. They are gitignored for
# the same reason on GitHub's side, nothing in the site references them, and
# they still need hosting or compression before they ship.
public/testimonials/*.mp4

# Build output and local state. Vercel builds from source, so sending these is
# at best wasted upload and at worst a stale build being served.
.git
node_modules
.next
.next-check
.vercel

# Local design mockups, gitignored as well.
design
